		(uuid "1a488a99-836b-5cec-b758-5e0213f61eed")
	)
	(text "Why: a current-source DUT cannot be held in CC (two current sources in series rail to\ncompliance), and a firmware CV loop on the DAC cannot either: 1 LSB into the 2.2 uF snubber\nslews 11 V in one 10 ms update. Here: V_DUT below CV_SET -> U12A rises -> Q13 pulls V_SET\ndown -> less current. CV_SET = 0 V: VSEN_OA (85 mV minimum) > CV_SET, U12A stays low, Q13\noff, plain CC (decks 01-04). Deck 06: settles for 0.1 - 8 A with and without 47 uF across\nthe DUT. Below 0.1 A it hunts: use CC or a resistor there."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.15 216.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84d57bf9-96ca-539f-89fa-5c7b6454266b")
	)
	(text "B   Hardware constant-voltage loop (LTspice deck 06)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.39 138.22 0)
